  "body": "**Stacked on #573** (#557 axes in the plane + #554 face-only plane picks). It includes #573's commits until that PR merges; upstream/main (v0.16.0) is merged in.\n\n## What changed\nA third way to lay the part on a work plane: through **three picked points** (#555).\n- **One apply path.** The face lay's core moved out of `pick/plane.rs` into a shared `lay_datum`. Both the face pick and the new `pick/points.rs::lay_on_points` go through it, and a test checks that a face and three of its corners give the same alignment for G17/G18/G19, with every flip and place combination.\n- **Outside side:** the side the material reaches less far into. Pick order doesn't matter for points on the hull. A plane through the middle of the part falls back to the 1→2→3 right-hand normal.\n- **Flip:** same meaning as in the face row.\n- **3-2-1 frame** (optional): after the lay, point 1→2 runs along the plane's first axis and point 1 goes to the setup origin. The work offset is never touched.\n- **With #557:** a later \"Axes in the plane\" pick turns on top of a three-point lay. The latest command wins.\n- **Command:** new `AlignPartToSetup::lay_on_points` / `check_points` entries. One undo step; ops go stale and undo clears that; stock and linked setups follow exactly as for the face lay.\n- **Refused by name:**\n  - not exactly three picks;\n  - a face or edge pick;\n  - a point off the part, or one that has gone;\n  - no model;\n  - a non-finite vertex;\n  - points closer than 0.001 mm;\n  - near-collinear points (least height under sin 1° × the longest side).\n- **Setup page:** a new row, \"Lay on a plane - pick three points\", under the face row.\n  - Prompts for Point 1, 2 and 3, with Remove last, Clear and **Apply points** (greyed with the reason).\n  - Controls for Flip, point 1 to plane level, and the 3-2-1 frame.\n  - Only one pick draft collects at a time.\n- **MCP:** a `lay_part_on_points` tool.\n- **Decision record:** `docs/decisions/555-three-point-plane.md`.\n\n## How tested\n- **app `points_align` (8):**\n  - a tilted face laid on G17 (normal −Z, z = 0, part above), independent of pick order;\n  - equal to face-to-plane;\n  - flip;\n  - the frame variant, including G19;\n  - each refusal by name;\n  - undo, redo and the \"already holds\" refusal;\n  - stock refits and stale/un-stale.\n- **MCP:** `lay_part_on_points_lays_the_plane_through_three_vertices`.\n- **UI:**\n  - `setup_points_tests` (2), driven by real clicks on the row, ending in Ctrl+Z/Ctrl+Y;\n  - `points_vertex_pick`: three real viewport clicks on the block's top corners make a valid plane;\n  - `structural` extended for the new row.\n- **Gate:** setup_align, plane_align(_edges), winding_align, axis_align, wcs_align, commands_undo, project_roundtrip, mcp_setup and the ui setup/plane/axis/points/structural tests pass. Clippy is clean. No snapshot PNGs were touched.\n\n**Deferred:**\n- Points on faces: a pick carries no hit point yet, so only model corners can be picked.\n- The non-finite-vertex refusal has no test, because no importer can produce such a vertex.\n\nChangelog: Setups page and MCP can lay the part on a G17/G18/G19 plane through three picked points (same apply path as face-to-plane, flip, optional 3-2-1 frame: point 1 origin, 1→2 along +X); collinear, coincident and off-part points refused by name (#555)\n\nFixes #555\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
